the number of positive integers which are divisible by $2^2=4$ less than or equal to $20$ is $\left \lfloor \dfrac{20}{4} \right \rfloor$;
the number of positive integers which are divisible by $2^3=8$ less than or equal to $20$ is $\left \lfloor \dfrac{20}{8} \right \rfloor$;

$20=8\cdot 2+4$


